registerEnglish([["Mark",1,1,"Wherefore the Sabbath was given unto man for a day of rest; and also that man should glorify God, and not that man should not eat;"],["Mark",1,2,"For the Son of man made the Sabbath day, therefore the Son of man is Lord also of the Sabbath."],["Mark",2,1,"And then came certain men unto him, accusing him, saying, Why do ye receive sinners, seeing thou makest thyself the Son of God."],["Mark",2,2,"But he answered them and said, Verily I say unto you, All sins which men have committed, when they repent, shall be forgiven them; for I came to preach repentance unto the sons of men."],["Mark",2,3,"And blasphemies, wherewith soever they shall blaspheme, shall be forgiven them that come unto me, and do the works which they see me do."],["Mark",2,4,"But there is a sin which shall not be forgiven. He that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost, hath never forgiveness; but is in danger of being cut down out of the world. And they shall inherit eternal damnation."],["Mark",2,5,"And this he said unto them because they said, He hath an unclean spirit."],["Mark",3,1,"Full well is it written of you, by the prophets whom ye have rejected."],["Mark",3,2,"They testified these things of a truth, and their blood shall be upon you."],["Mark",3,3,"Ye have kept not the ordinances of God; for Moses said, Honor thy father and thy mother; and whoso curseth father or mother, let him die the death of the transgressor, as it is written in your law; but ye keep not the law."],["Mark",4,1,"For whosoever will save his life, shall lose it; or whosoever will save his life, shall be willing to lay it down for my sake; and if he is not willing to lay it down for my sake, he shall lose it."],["Mark",4,2,"But whosoever shall be willing to lose his life for my sake, and the gospel, the same shall save it."],["Mark",4,3,"And they shall not have part in that resurrection when he cometh."],["Mark",4,4,"For verily I say unto you, That he shall come; and he that layeth down his life for my sake and the gospel’s, shall come with him, and shall be clothed with his glory in the cloud, on the right hand of the Son of man."],["Mark",5,1,"And there appeared unto them Elias with Moses, or in other words, John the Baptist and Moses; and they were talking with Jesus."],["Mark",5,2,"Therefore, if thy hand offend thee, cut it off; or if thy brother offend thee and confess not and forsake not, he shall be cut off. It is better for thee to enter into life maimed, than having two hands, to go into hell."],["Mark",5,3,"For it is better for thee to enter into life without thy brother, than for thee and thy brother to be cast into hell; into the fire that never shall be quenched, where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched."],["Mark",5,4,"And again, if thy foot offend thee, cut it off; for he that is thy standard, by whom thou walkest, if he become a transgressor, he shall be cut off."],["Mark",6,1,"He is not therefore the God of the dead, but the God of the living; for he raiseth them up out of their graves. Ye therefore do greatly err."],["Mark",7,1,"And as they did eat, Jesus took bread and blessed it, and brake, and gave to them, and said, Take it, and eat."],["Mark",7,2,"Behold, this is for you to do in remembrance of my body; for as oft as ye do this ye will remember this hour that I was with you."],["Mark",7,3,"And he took the cup, and when he had given thanks, he gave it to them; and they all drank of it."],["Mark",7,4,"And he said unto them, This is in remembrance of my blood which is shed for many, and the new testament which I give unto you; for of me ye shall bear record unto all the world."],["Mark",7,5,"And as oft as ye do this ordinance, ye will remember me in this hour that I was with you and drank with you of this cup, even the last time in my ministry."],["Mark",7,6,"Verily I say unto you, Of this ye shall bear record; for I will no more drink of the fruit of the vine with you, until that day that I drink it new in the kingdom of God."],["Mark",7,7,"And now they were grieved, and wept over him."],["Mark",8,1,"But when they looked, they saw that the stone was rolled away, (for it was very great,) and two angels sitting thereon, clothed in long white garments; and they were affrighted."],["Mark",8,2,"But the angels said unto them, Be not affrighted; ye seek Jesus of Nazareth, who was crucified; he is risen; he is not here; behold the place where they laid him;"],["Mark",8,3,"And go your way, tell his disciples and Peter, that he goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him as he said unto you."],["Mark",8,4,"And they, entering into the sepulcher, saw the place where they laid Jesus."]]);
